From ab193249a1a7cba5bdb5eb00bc298721e61a608d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:12:48 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Test: the source snapshot reaches psi_star[0] inside a
 named expression

With the source snapshot enabled, the commit projection of a flux history
reads a frozen copy of psi_star[0]. The substitution did not reach an
occurrence held inside a UWexpression (E_eff_inv_II at yield), which kept
reading the history live. The commit's check that the copy equals the
history kept every result right, so the test makes them differ on purpose
and solves the projection directly: on development the diagonal, read
through the named expression, is 1.0 off, and psi_star[0] is left in the
compiled source (UNFILED 11). A third case pins a named quantity with
units (a viscosity in Pa s), which holds no psi_star[0] and must be left as
it is. A fourth builds the source through a diamond of shared named
expressions 16 levels deep, under a 2 s bound: a walk without a memo took
37 s here, a walk with one 0.4 s.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
